WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.434
-He is an Emmy-nominated
actor and writer --

00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:04.868
David, were you Emmy-nominated?

00:00:04.868 --> 00:00:07.267
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:07.267 --> 00:00:08.467
Actor and writer.

00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:12.133
He's a very funny comedian with

00:00:12.133 --> 00:00:13.901
a brand-new stand-up
special called

00:00:13.901 --> 00:00:16.133
"David Spade: Nothing Personal,"

00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:17.834
which is streaming now
on Netflix.

00:00:17.834 --> 00:00:21.801
Please welcome the
always-entertaining David Spade!

00:00:21.801 --> 00:00:23.601
-♪ Nothin', nothin', nothin',

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:27.033
nothin',
nothin', nothin', nothin' ♪

00:00:27.033 --> 00:00:29.033
♪ Nothin', nothin', nothin',

00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:32.534
nothin',
nothin', nothin', nothin' ♪

00:00:32.534 --> 00:00:35.367
♪ Nothin', nothin', nothin'... ♪

00:00:35.367 --> 00:00:37.133
-That's exactly right.

00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:38.601
That's exactly right.

00:00:38.601 --> 00:00:40.767
-That's more like it.
-Yeah.

00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:43.100
Standing ovation for
Mr. David Spade.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.234
-Yes.
-Absolutely right, buddy.

00:00:44.234 --> 00:00:45.367
We love you.

00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:46.901
-Jimmy, I have
a stupid question for you.

00:00:46.901 --> 00:00:48.133
-What's up?

00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:49.801
-This is so --
And I'm so embarrassed.

00:00:49.801 --> 00:00:51.200
-Yeah.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.067
-You're Jimmy Kimmel or Fallon?

00:00:53.067 --> 00:00:54.234
-Oh, my God.
-Fallon.

00:00:54.234 --> 00:00:56.367
-Your microphone is on, yeah.
-Oh, Fallon.

00:00:56.367 --> 00:00:57.734
No, and I knew that,

00:00:57.734 --> 00:01:00.200
but then I said backstage,
and two people weren't sure.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:04.734
And then -- But I always say
"Jimmy, Jimmy," but I never --

00:01:04.734 --> 00:01:06.200
-You don't know the last name.
-No, I don't.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:08.234
But you know what? I know now.
-Yeah.

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:10.367
I got to say, I had dinner
with you last night.

00:01:10.367 --> 00:01:12.267
I'm very --
When you come into town,

00:01:12.267 --> 00:01:14.634
I'm lucky enough you invite
me out to --

00:01:14.634 --> 00:01:16.801
-I know. There's few people
I like to eat with.

00:01:16.801 --> 00:01:19.934
You're always hilarious,
fun to go out with.

00:01:19.934 --> 00:01:21.901
Chris Rock came. We --

00:01:21.901 --> 00:01:22.968
-Yeah, me, you,
and Chris Rock is interesting

00:01:22.968 --> 00:01:26.667
to sit with each other,
because --

00:01:26.667 --> 00:01:27.968
Chris came a little bit later,

00:01:27.968 --> 00:01:29.167
so, at first,
it was just me and you.

00:01:29.167 --> 00:01:30.234
-Yeah.

00:01:30.234 --> 00:01:31.701
-And do you remember,

00:01:31.701 --> 00:01:33.601
there's one nice lady
who was leaving,

00:01:33.601 --> 00:01:35.801
and she goes,
"David Spade, oh, my God,

00:01:35.801 --> 00:01:37.367
you're the funniest person
on Earth."

00:01:37.367 --> 00:01:39.100
-Oh, yeah, yeah.
-And I go...

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:41.501
-I know.
No, but she liked you, too.

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:42.567
-Yeah, then she said
something like,

00:01:42.567 --> 00:01:44.501
"You're okay, too" of something.

00:01:44.501 --> 00:01:46.234
-She goes,
"And you're doing your thing."

00:01:46.234 --> 00:01:48.601
-I'm like, "Yeah, whatever."
And then Chris comes in.

00:01:48.601 --> 00:01:49.667
-I know.

00:01:49.667 --> 00:01:52.501
And then it was,
like, over, yeah.

00:01:52.501 --> 00:01:55.534
-Then people were judging us.
People were going in order.

00:01:55.534 --> 00:01:57.100
They're like,
"Okay, you're kind of funny."

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:59.667
-"If we go by TV..."

00:01:59.667 --> 00:02:00.968
But Chris was great.

00:02:00.968 --> 00:02:03.267
You know, also,
that place was so nice.

00:02:03.267 --> 00:02:05.067
-Polo Bar.
-Yes.

00:02:05.067 --> 00:02:07.234
And they --
But, you know, sometimes,

00:02:07.234 --> 00:02:08.334
they try to up-charge you.

00:02:08.334 --> 00:02:09.968
Not that restaurant,
but other ones.

00:02:09.968 --> 00:02:12.567
And -- But, like,
you know, they're like,

00:02:12.567 --> 00:02:14.734
"Hey, you want some truffles
in your Diet Coke?"

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.501
"No."

00:02:16.501 --> 00:02:17.667
"Alright."

00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:19.000
-Well, they know who
they're dealing with.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:20.434
Yeah, it's David Spade.
-They give it like you're cheap.

00:02:20.434 --> 00:02:22.567
They're like, "Okay.

00:02:22.567 --> 00:02:25.100
$35 Diet Coke.
Is that a problem for you?"

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:27.667
-But you're a comedy beast.

00:02:27.667 --> 00:02:29.701
You went -- You and Chris
went and did stand-up,

00:02:29.701 --> 00:02:30.968
surprised the audience at the...

00:02:30.968 --> 00:02:32.000
-The Comedy Cellar.
-...the Cellar last night.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.100
-Yeah, that was great.

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:35.167
You know, when I come in,
we, you know --

00:02:35.167 --> 00:02:36.667
And it always happens
every time,

00:02:36.667 --> 00:02:39.501
and then, at the end of dinner,
he goes, "Wanna go do a set?"

00:02:39.501 --> 00:02:40.934
-Yeah.

00:02:40.934 --> 00:02:43.434
-But he's on tour right now,
and I'm on tour for once.

00:02:43.434 --> 00:02:47.067
So we go out on the road,
and so he's super-polished.

00:02:47.067 --> 00:02:48.234
He crushed it.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:49.767
-How was the crowd last night?

00:02:49.767 --> 00:02:51.234
-They were great.

00:02:51.234 --> 00:02:52.667
You know, you walk in, and the
Comedy Cellar is a great room,

00:02:52.667 --> 00:02:53.868
so we just go on --

00:02:53.868 --> 00:02:55.534
-I mean, you're on tour now.
Do you love it?

00:02:55.534 --> 00:02:57.033
-I'm -- Yeah.

00:02:57.033 --> 00:02:59.334
You know, I haven't really done
a theater tour in a long time,

00:02:59.334 --> 00:03:01.567
so it's a little rigmarole.

00:03:01.567 --> 00:03:03.534
But, oh, you know what happened?
This is exciting.

00:03:03.534 --> 00:03:07.400
I was -- Not really.
But I was...

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:08.901
-By the way,
this is exactly like

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:10.434
having dinner with David Spade

00:03:10.434 --> 00:03:12.901
It's so many jokes.
-It's really bits ahoy.

00:03:12.901 --> 00:03:14.367
-I love it.
It's bits ahoy for both of us.

00:03:14.367 --> 00:03:15.801
I love it.
-So, we go.

00:03:15.801 --> 00:03:18.067
So, here I am flying, and then
the stewardess comes out --

00:03:18.067 --> 00:03:19.934
The flight attendant comes out.

00:03:19.934 --> 00:03:21.634
And she goes,
"It's a little scary."

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:22.667
She goes,
"I have an announcement."

00:03:22.667 --> 00:03:24.901
And then we're all like,
"Uh-oh."

00:03:24.901 --> 00:03:26.634
And she goes,
"There's a bomb on the plane."

00:03:26.634 --> 00:03:28.901
Then she goes, "No, no.
It's good news. It's good news."

00:03:28.901 --> 00:03:31.267
And, you know, I like her
to have a little personality.

00:03:31.267 --> 00:03:34.334
And, so, she goes,
"Take your masks off.

00:03:34.334 --> 00:03:36.234
They just announced you don't
have to wear your mask."

00:03:36.234 --> 00:03:38.367
And then she had garbage,
and she threw it in.

00:03:38.367 --> 00:03:39.467
And then she goes,
"Take 'em off."

00:03:39.467 --> 00:03:40.501
And we were all like,
"Whoo-hoo!"

00:03:40.501 --> 00:03:41.901
And everyone did it.

00:03:41.901 --> 00:03:43.501
And then I go, "Oh, wait.

00:03:43.501 --> 00:03:45.267
I need it in the airport."

00:03:45.267 --> 00:03:48.367
So, I was like...

00:03:48.367 --> 00:03:49.400
-"I remember which one
was mine."

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:50.534
-It was.

00:03:50.534 --> 00:03:52.534
It was a little bit of a
grab-bag situation.

00:03:52.534 --> 00:03:55.033
I was like, "Eh, this one fits.

00:03:55.033 --> 00:03:57.167
Little perfumey, but, you know,

00:03:57.167 --> 00:04:00.334
just for that half-mile
to the luggage."

00:04:00.334 --> 00:04:01.467
So, that was good.

00:04:01.467 --> 00:04:02.901
Then I get out of the plane.
Oh, wait.

00:04:02.901 --> 00:04:04.601
Actually, on the plane,
when I took it off,

00:04:04.601 --> 00:04:06.467
this guy next to me --
You realize people

00:04:06.467 --> 00:04:08.734
don't know
because you're kind of hidden.

00:04:08.734 --> 00:04:10.601
And he goes, "Hey, man."

00:04:10.601 --> 00:04:11.968
And I go, "Oh, hey, dude."

00:04:11.968 --> 00:04:13.300
And he goes, "Oh, that was you?"

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:14.734
I go, "You didn't know
for three hours?

00:04:14.734 --> 00:04:17.467
I'm talking. I'm standing.
I'm right next to you, across."

00:04:17.467 --> 00:04:18.934
And he goes, "Ah, no."

00:04:18.934 --> 00:04:21.400
And I go, "I have
a 'Grown Ups' coat on.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:25.534
I have an 'Emperor's New Groove'
lunchbox. Nothing?"

00:04:25.534 --> 00:04:27.000
And he's like, "No."
-"Saturday Night Live."

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:28.234
-Yeah. He goes,
"I know 'Joe Dirt.'"

00:04:28.234 --> 00:04:29.534
I go, "Oh, okay."

00:04:29.534 --> 00:04:33.901
So, I get off and then I go,
and then the first guy --

00:04:33.901 --> 00:04:35.734
You know,
it was an early flight.

00:04:35.734 --> 00:04:37.267
And I go to one of those
little bagel stores

00:04:37.267 --> 00:04:39.801
where they have a table
that's a like circle

00:04:39.801 --> 00:04:41.434
like this big, you know?

00:04:41.434 --> 00:04:42.767
Fits one.

00:04:42.767 --> 00:04:45.200
And there's no chairs because
they want you to beat it.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:47.400
So, I have a little bagel
and I'm like...

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:48.801
just grossly eating a bagel.

00:04:48.801 --> 00:04:50.634
And then a guy comes
and stands next to me

00:04:50.634 --> 00:04:52.300
and scooches his bagel
next to mine.

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:53.334
Errrr!

00:04:53.334 --> 00:04:54.968
Like, it doesn't even fit
two barely.

00:04:54.968 --> 00:04:56.400
And I go...

00:04:56.400 --> 00:05:00.834
And he goes, "A little
A.M. bagel in the morning."

00:05:00.834 --> 00:05:02.901
Like, the most crammed-in talk.

00:05:02.901 --> 00:05:04.234
I go, "Yeah."

00:05:04.234 --> 00:05:08.501
And he goes, "Yeah, I'm doing a
little bagelage myself."

00:05:08.501 --> 00:05:09.834
And then I go, "Okay."

00:05:09.834 --> 00:05:14.100
And then he goes, "Bagel time
U.S.A." or something.

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:17.200
I go -- And then I kind of
started fading out.

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:20.000
And then he goes,
"Alright, bagel it up, dude."

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.868
-Oh, my God.
-And then that was it.

00:05:21.868 --> 00:05:24.100
And I go, "Did we just talk?
I don't know what happened."

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:26.133
-Wow. Doing a little bagelage.

00:05:26.133 --> 00:05:27.634
-And then I went
to the Sunglass Hut.

00:05:27.634 --> 00:05:28.968
And then I'm gonna let you
talk in a second.

00:05:28.968 --> 00:05:31.968
But I went to Sunglass Hut.

00:05:31.968 --> 00:05:34.100
Is it Sunglasses or Sunglass?

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:36.400
-I say Sunglass Hut.
-Yeah, I say that.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:38.901
So -- And, by the way,
it was bumpin'.

00:05:38.901 --> 00:05:42.100
And there were so many people
buying sunglasses.

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:43.434
And then I thought,
"You know what?

00:05:43.434 --> 00:05:44.534
They're doing so well,

00:05:44.534 --> 00:05:46.267
they should have
a building now."

00:05:46.267 --> 00:05:49.534
Yeah, forget the hut.
We're moving out of that.

00:05:49.534 --> 00:05:51.934
-No more hut.
Take a step above the hut.

00:05:51.934 --> 00:05:55.400
-Yeah, get a building.
You know, commit.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:56.534
-Sunglass Hut.

00:05:56.534 --> 00:05:59.634
-That's not in the special.
Don't worry.

00:05:59.634 --> 00:06:01.400
I give you the duds here,

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:05.100
but the special is
all the cream of the crop.

00:06:06.767 --> 00:06:08.367
-Besides your stand-up tour,

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:10.868
you're also doing
a very funny podcast.

00:06:10.868 --> 00:06:13.067
-Oh, yeah, with Dana.
-The one-and-only Dana Carvey.

00:06:13.067 --> 00:06:14.901
-Dana Carvey --
give him some applause.

00:06:14.901 --> 00:06:17.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
-"Fly on the Wall."

00:06:17.634 --> 00:06:19.701
It's called "Fly on the Wall."
-Yeah.

00:06:19.701 --> 00:06:21.634
-And how did
the podcast come about?

00:06:21.634 --> 00:06:23.601
-Well, Dana and I, you know,
we're on the show.

00:06:23.601 --> 00:06:25.767
We sort of overlap --
We didn't overlap with you.

00:06:25.767 --> 00:06:27.367
But he was on before me,

00:06:27.367 --> 00:06:28.834
and then we overlapped
and we were buddies.

00:06:28.834 --> 00:06:30.400
And then we
live near each other,

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:31.601
and then I try to get him --

00:06:31.601 --> 00:06:32.934
drag him out to
dinner sometimes.

00:06:32.934 --> 00:06:35.701
And we have a lot of laughs.
He's super-funny dude.

00:06:35.701 --> 00:06:37.234
And we talk "SNL" stuff.

00:06:37.234 --> 00:06:40.267
And then, like, someone we know
from "SNL" will come to dinner.

00:06:40.267 --> 00:06:41.367
And we talked about this.

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:43.467
I go, "You know,
you have to do a podcast.

00:06:43.467 --> 00:06:45.400
You know, it's sort of like
jury duty."

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:49.534
So we said, "Let's do one,
and then maybe we'll do

00:06:49.534 --> 00:06:50.901
a sort of 'SNL' slant to it,

00:06:50.901 --> 00:06:52.834
because all of our friends
are on there."

00:06:52.834 --> 00:06:55.734
So we did that.
And it's pretty funny.

00:06:55.734 --> 00:06:57.300
We actually did a live one.

00:06:57.300 --> 00:06:59.267
We did a live one in Austin.
It's so funny.

00:06:59.267 --> 00:07:01.667
It's a 2,800-seat theater,

00:07:01.667 --> 00:07:03.334
and it's just
three guys talking.

00:07:03.334 --> 00:07:05.834
You know, it's not like
Ringling Bros., you know?

00:07:05.834 --> 00:07:08.634
So I get scared, but the crowd
was super into it.

00:07:08.634 --> 00:07:11.367
And then we're doing one in L.A.
next week with Sandler.

00:07:11.367 --> 00:07:13.234
He's going to be our guest.
So, it's like -- It's all fun.

00:07:13.234 --> 00:07:16.634
Just goofing around.
-I heard -- I know Tina was on.

00:07:16.634 --> 00:07:17.801
-Tina was on.

00:07:17.801 --> 00:07:18.868
-Basically everyone from
"Saturday Night Live."

00:07:18.868 --> 00:07:21.334
-Mike Myers is this week.
We had Tom Hanks.

00:07:21.334 --> 00:07:22.701
-Yeah, a lot of great people.

00:07:22.701 --> 00:07:25.601
-Yeah, everyone -- You're --
I want you on.

00:07:25.601 --> 00:07:27.300
-Yeah, where's that invite?

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:28.901
-No, but it's just -- Right now,
it's a little tricky.

00:07:28.901 --> 00:07:31.100
-Right now, you're booked.
-No, no.

00:07:31.100 --> 00:07:33.634
I -- Yeah, I'm going to
have you on,

00:07:33.634 --> 00:07:35.968
but I just want to make sure
we got an hour of stuff.

00:07:35.968 --> 00:07:39.234
[ Laughter ]

00:07:39.234 --> 00:07:40.467
I've got to feel it out.
-I've got to work my way up.

00:07:40.467 --> 00:07:41.601
Yeah.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:07:41.601 --> 00:07:43.000
-I want to talk about your
stand-up special,

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:44.167
"Nothing Personal," on Netflix.

00:07:44.167 --> 00:07:45.167
More with David Spade
when we come back.

00:07:45.167 --> 00:07:46.300
-Oh, more!

